## 3️⃣  Put it all together – a minimal HTML page

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <title>MapLibre GL JS – cache:// protocol demo</title>
  <style>
    #map { position: absolute; top:0; bottom:0; left:0; right:0; }
  </style>
  <!-- MapLibre GL JS v4.x (or newer) -->
  <script src="https://unpkg.com/maplibre-gl@4.4.0/dist/maplibre-gl.js"></script>
  <link href="https://unpkg.com/maplibre-gl@4.4.0/dist/maplibre-gl.css" rel="stylesheet"/>
</head>
<body>
<div id="map"></div>

<script type="module">
  // ---- 1️⃣  Import the helpers we just wrote ----
  import { registerCacheProtocol } from './protocol.js';

  // ---- 2️⃣  Register the protocol BEFORE creating the map ----
  registerCacheProtocol();

  // ---- 3️⃣  Create the map ----
  const map = new maplibregl.Map({
    container: 'map',
    style: {
      version: 8,
      sources: {
        // The source uses our custom scheme.
        // The URL pattern must match what the handler expects.
        myTiles: {
          type: 'vector',
          // Note the trailing slash – MapLibre will replace {z}/{x}/{y}
          // automatically when it builds the request URL.
          url: 'cache://tiles/'
        }
      },
      layers: [
        {
          id: 'water',
          type: 'fill',
          source: 'myTiles',
          'source-layer': 'water', // <-- name of the layer inside the MVT
          paint: { 'fill-color': '#a0c8f0' }
        }
        // …add more layers that reference the same source if you like
      ]
    },
    center: [0, 0],
    zoom: 2,
    // optional: keep the map from trying to load the default style
    // (we are providing a full style object above)
    hash: true
  });

  map.on('error', (e) => console.error('MapLibre error:', e));
</script>
</body>
</html>
```

### What the code does

| Step | What happens |
|------|--------------|
| **`registerCacheProtocol()`** | Calls `maplibregl.addProtocol('cache', handler)`. From now on every request whose URL starts with `cache://` is handed to `handler`. |
| **`handler`** | Parses the `{z}/{x}/{y}` part, opens (or creates) the IndexedDB `tile-cache`, looks for a cached tile, and if missing fetches it from a remote HTTP endpoint, stores it, and returns the raw `ArrayBuffer`. |
| **Style** | The source URL `cache://tiles/` tells MapLibre to request tiles like `cache://tiles/12/3456/7890`. The handler receives the full URL, extracts the numbers, and serves the tile. |
| **Result** | The map renders exactly as if you had used a normal `https://…` source, but after the first request each tile lives locally in IndexedDB, so subsequent loads are **offline-first**. |

